hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"34","On reciting Bismillah aloud. Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sharik, from Salim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim aloud in Makkah. He said: The people of Makkah used to call Musaylimah al-Rahman, so they said: Muhammad is calling upon the god of Yamamah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded and concealed it, and he never recited it aloud until he died."
"35","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Husayn, from Abu Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to write: In Your name, O Allah. Then, when: Indeed, it is from Sulayman, and indeed, it is in the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate - was revealed, he wrote: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"36","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not know the end of a surah until Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim was revealed. Abu Dawud said: This hadith has been given a connected chain, and this is more correct."
